Title: 0003-aros-locale-setter-noop
Repository: skia
Base-Commit: 588b550a4dd8af90dbe71c0554852806bd8f0b21
Requires: 0001-aros-posix-file-memory.patch
Author: aros-skia
Date: 2026-09-24
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: src/core/SkAutoLocaleSetter.h. AROS x86_64 ABIv11. Not checked on mainline v1.

Problem:
  SkAutoLocaleSetter switches the calling thread to the "C" locale with
  newlocale(LC_ALL_MASK)/uselocale while Ganesh generates GLSL and
  SkJSONReader parses numbers, so float formatting uses '.'. ABIv11 posixc
  declares locale_t but has no newlocale, uselocale, freelocale or
  LC_ALL_MASK; the file does not compile.
Solution:
  Take Skia's existing no-op branch (HAVE_LOCALE_T 0, as for Android,
  uClibc and newlib). This keeps the class's contract rather than
  approximating it: AROS stdc formats and parses numbers in the C locale
  unconditionally. printf's decimal point is the constant "."
  (compiler/crt/stdc/__vcformat.c: __stdc_char_decimalpoint,
  FMTPRINTF_DECIMALPOINT) and strtod accepts only '.' (strtod.c), whatever
  setlocale() was given. Nothing global is changed, so there is no
  cross-thread effect; a process-wide setlocale() substitute was rejected
  for exactly that reason.
Validation:
  GCC 13.4.0, ABIv11 SDK: the users of SkAutoLocaleSetter.h
  (GrGLProgramBuilder.cpp, SkJSONReader.cpp) compile, and the gl example,
  which generates GLSL through GrGLProgramBuilder, passes on AROS One.
  Source references checked in deadwood2/AROS e33ca77d.
Removal:
  When posixc provides newlocale/uselocale, or when AROS stdc gains a
  locale-dependent decimal point (then this no-op would become wrong and a
  real per-thread setter is needed).

diff --git a/src/core/SkAutoLocaleSetter.h b/src/core/SkAutoLocaleSetter.h
index 4642ca2..89cfa11 100644
--- a/src/core/SkAutoLocaleSetter.h
+++ b/src/core/SkAutoLocaleSetter.h
@@ -27,7 +27,8 @@
 #define HAVE_XLOCALE 0
 #endif
 
-#if defined(SK_BUILD_FOR_ANDROID) || defined(__UCLIBC__) || defined(_NEWLIB_VERSION)
+#if defined(SK_BUILD_FOR_ANDROID) || defined(__UCLIBC__) || defined(_NEWLIB_VERSION) || \
+    defined(__AROS__)
 #define HAVE_LOCALE_T 0
 #else
 #define HAVE_LOCALE_T 1
